# 🛡️ Agent Safety Guardrail (.cursorrules)
# Policy specification loaded automatically by Cursor Agent & Composer

You must strictly adhere to the safety guardrail defined in policy.yaml:

1. BLOCK (Refuse immediately — never retry by rephrasing, splitting, or encoding):
   - Never run recursive file deletions (rm -rf, rmdir /s, Remove-Item -Recurse -Force).
   - Never force-push or delete branches on remote git repositories (git push -f, git push --force, git reset --hard).
   - Never execute SQL drops/truncations (DROP TABLE, TRUNCATE, DELETE without WHERE).
   - Never print, export, exfiltrate, or commit secrets (.env, API keys, private keys, certificates).
   - Never modify or disable guardrail control files (policy.yaml, check_action.py, guardrail_hook.py, mcp_server.py, .cursorrules).

2. ASK USER (Request explicit human confirmation in the current turn before running):
   - Modifications to .env, docker-compose.yml, Dockerfile, or production configs.
   - Container executions: docker run, docker exec, docker compose up/down.
   - Kubernetes / Cloud mutations: kubectl apply/delete, terraform apply.
   - Global package installations (npm i -g, pip install --user).

3. PROCEED (Execute silently):
   - Read-only commands: ls, dir, cat, grep, git status, git diff, git log.
   - Test suites and linters: pytest, npm test, cargo test, ruff, eslint, mypy.
   - Routine code edits within the workspace.

Before executing any non-read-only command, verify it via the `agent-guardrail` MCP `check_action` tool or run:
python check_action.py "<command>" --json
